 } } \right]$$ and M = A + A2 + A3 + ....... + A20, then the sum of all the elements of the matrix M is equal to _____________.

The number of distinct real roots 

of $$\left| {\matrix{
   {\sin x} &amp; {\cos x} &amp; {\cos x}  \cr 
   {\cos x} &amp; {\sin x} &amp; {\cos x}  \cr 
   {\cos x} &amp; {\cos x} &amp; {\sin x}  \cr 

 } } \right| = 0$$ in the interval $$ - {\pi  \over 4} \le x \le {\pi  \over 4}$$ is :

explanation:
$$\left| {\matrix{
   {\sin x} &amp; {\cos x} &amp; {\cos x}  \cr 
   {\cos x} &amp; {\sin x} &amp; {\cos x}  \cr 
   {\cos x} &amp; {\cos x} &amp; {\sin x}  \cr 

 } } \right| = 0, - {\pi  \over 4} \le x \le {\pi  \over 4}$$

Apply : $${R_1} \to {R_1} - {R_2}$$ &amp; $${R_2} \to {R_2} - {R_3}$$

$$ \Rightarrow $$ $$\left| {\matrix{
   {\sin x - \cos x} &amp; {\cos x - \sin x} &amp; 0  \cr 
   0 &amp; {\sin x - \cos x} &amp; {\cos x - \sin x}  \cr 
   {\cos x} &amp; {\cos x} &amp; {\sin x}  \cr 

 } } \right| = 0$$

$$ \Rightarrow $$ $${(\sin x - \cos x)^2}\left| {\matrix{
   1 &amp; { - 1} &amp; 0  \cr 
   0 &amp; 1 &amp; { - 1}  \cr 
   {\cos x} &amp; {\cos x} &amp; {\sin x}  \cr 

 } } \right| = 0$$

$$ \Rightarrow $$ $${(\sin x - \cos x)^2}(\sin x + 2\cos x) = 0$$

$$\therefore$$ $$x = {\pi  \over 4}$$

