 } } \right] + \left[ {\matrix{
   0 & 0 & {{{n(n - 1)ab} \over 2}}  \cr 
   0 & 0 & 0  \cr 
   0 & 0 & 0  \cr 

 } } \right]$$
$$ = \left[ {\matrix{
   1 & {na} & {na + {{n(n - 1)} \over 2}ab}  \cr 
   0 & 1 & {nb}  \cr 
   0 & 0 & 1  \cr 

 } } \right] = \left[ {\matrix{
   1 & {48} & {2160}  \cr 
   0 & 1 & {48}  \cr 
   0 & 0 & 1  \cr 

 } } \right]$$
On comparing we get $$na = 48$$, $$nb = 96$$ and
$$na + {{n(n - 1)} \over 2}ab = 2160$$
$$ \Rightarrow a = 4,n = 12$$ and $$b = 8$$
$$n + a + b = 24$$

