Let A be a symmetric matrix such that $$\mathrm{|A|=2}$$ and $$\left[ {\matrix{
   2 & 1  \cr 
   3 & {{3 \over 2}}  \cr 

 } } \right]A = \left[ {\matrix{
   1 & 2  \cr 
   \alpha  & \beta   \cr 

 } } \right]$$. If the sum of the diagonal elements of A is $$s$$, then $$\frac{\beta s}{\alpha^2}$$ is equal to __________.

explanation:
$$A = \left( {\matrix{
   a & c  \cr 
   c & b  \cr 

 } } \right)$$
$$|A| = ab - {c^2} = 2$$ ...... (1)
$$\left( {\matrix{
