Given, $A B$ be a vertical wall of height $30 \mathrm{~m}$ and $P Q$ be a vertical tower.


Such that $\angle B Q A=\angle T A Q=60^{\circ}$ (Alternate angles)


and $\angle C P A=\angle T A P=15^{\circ}$





Now, $\tan 60^{\circ}=\frac{A B}{B Q}=\frac{30}{B Q}$


$$
\begin{array}{ll}
&amp;\Rightarrow  \sqrt{3}=\frac{30}{B Q} \\\\
&amp;\Rightarrow  B Q=\frac{30}{\sqrt{3}}=10 \sqrt{3}
\end{array}
$$


$$
\begin{aligned}
&amp; \text { and } \tan 15^{\circ}=\frac{A C}{P C} \\\\
&amp; \Rightarrow 2-\sqrt{3}=\frac{A C}{10 \sqrt{3}} (\because P C=B Q) \\\\
&amp; \Rightarrow A C=10 \sqrt{3}(2-\sqrt{3})=20 \sqrt{3}-30 \\\\
&amp; \therefore B C=A B-A C=30-(20 \sqrt{3}-30)=60-20 \sqrt{3}
\end{aligned}
$$


$\therefore$ Area of quadrilateral $B C P Q$


$$
\begin{aligned}
