$$(p \to q) \wedge (q \to  \sim p)$$

$$ \equiv ( \sim p \vee q) \wedge ( \sim q \vee  \sim p)\{ p \to q \equiv  \sim p \vee q\} $$

$$ \equiv ( \sim p \vee q) \wedge ( \sim p \vee q)$$ {commutative property}

$$ \equiv  \sim p \vee (q \wedge  \sim q)$$ {distributive property}

$$ \equiv  \sim p$$

Converse of $((\sim p) \wedge q) \Rightarrow r$


$$
\begin{aligned}
& \equiv \mathrm{r} \Rightarrow(\sim \mathrm{p} \wedge \mathrm{q}) \\\\
