u_2}{3 	imes 10^{15}} =  rac{\left( rac{8}{9}ight)}{\left( rac{3}{4}ight)} =  rac{32}{27}$$Thus, to find the frequency $
u_2$ for the transition from $n=3$ to $n=1$:$$
u_2 =  rac{32}{9} 	imes 10^{15} \mathrm{Hz}$$Hence, in the given formula $ rac{x}{9} 	imes 10^{15} \mathrm{~Hz}$ for the frequency, $x$ is equal to $32$.

